> API and interpretation

The canonical producer and full-width guards were already implemented during the
non-restoring/Newton conversion; this report reuses them. It processes all64
bits, including leading-zero prefixes. The original figure selects the last
eight actual records and names that selection explicitly. Zero divisor preserves
a legacy{0,0,0}sentinel accompanied by valid_divisor=false; it is not a defined
division result. Hypothetical trial restores are a comparison with a different
hardware formulation, not executed additions or measured wasted work. Exact
full-width identities are checked with widened independent integer arithmetic.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

